### Configure AWS S3 Object Resource

Source: https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.33.0/website/docs/cdktf/python/r/s3_object.html.markdown

This section details the arguments available for defining and managing an S3 object using the `aws_s3_object` Terraform resource. It covers required parameters like bucket and key, as well as optional settings for ACLs, encryption, caching, and metadata.

```APIDOC
## RESOURCE aws_s3_object

### Description
Manages an S3 object within an AWS S3 bucket. This resource allows you to upload files, set metadata, configure access control, and manage encryption settings for objects stored in S3.

### Method
CREATE/UPDATE

### Resource Name
aws_s3_object

### Arguments
#### Required Arguments
- **bucket** (string) - Required - Name of the bucket to put the file in. Alternatively, an [S3 access point](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/using-access-points.html) ARN can be specified.
- **key** (string) - Required - Name of the object once it is in the bucket.

#### Optional Arguments
- **acl** (string) - Optional - [Canned ACL](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/acl-overview.html#canned-acl) to apply. Valid values are `private`, `public-read`, `public-read-write`, `aws-exec-read`, `authenticated-read`, `bucket-owner-read`, and `bucket-owner-full-control`.
- **bucket_key_enabled** (boolean) - Optional - Whether or not to use [Amazon S3 Bucket Keys](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/bucket-key.html) for SSE-KMS.
- **cache_control** (string) - Optional - Caching behavior along the request/reply chain. Read [w3c cache_control](http://www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec14.html#sec14.9) for further details.
- **checksum_algorithm** (string) - Optional - Indicates the algorithm used to create the checksum for the object. If a value is specified and the object is encrypted with KMS, you must have permission to use the `kms:Decrypt` action. Valid values: `CRC32`, `CRC32C`, `CRC64NVME`, `SHA1`, `SHA256`.
- **content_base64** (string) - Optional, conflicts with `source` and `content` - Base64-encoded data that will be decoded and uploaded as raw bytes for the object content. This allows safely uploading non-UTF8 binary data, but is recommended only for small content such as the result of the `gzipbase64` function with small text strings. For larger objects, use `source` to stream the content from a disk file.
- **content_disposition** (string) - Optional - Presentational information for the object. Read [w3c content_disposition](http://www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec19.1.html#sec19.5.1) for further information.
- **content_encoding** (string) - Optional - Content encodings that have been applied to the object and thus what decoding mechanisms must be applied to obtain the media-type referenced by the Content-Type header field. Read [w3c content encoding](http://www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec14.1.html#sec14.11) for further information.
- **content_language** (string) - Optional - Language the content is in e.g., en-US or en-GB.
- **content_type** (string) - Optional - Standard MIME type describing the format of the object data, e.g., application/octet-stream. All Valid MIME Types are valid for this input.
- **content** (string) - Optional, conflicts with `source` and `content_base64` - Literal string value to use as the object content, which will be uploaded as UTF-8-encoded text.
- **etag** (string) - Optional - Triggers updates when the value changes. The only meaningful value is `filemd5("path/to/file")` (Terraform 0.11.12 or later) or `${md5(file("path/to/file"))}` (Terraform 0.11.11 or earlier). This attribute is not compatible with KMS encryption, `kms_key_id` or `server_side_encryption = "aws:kms"`, also if an object is larger than 16 MB, the AWS Management Console will upload or copy that object as a Multipart Upload, and therefore the ETag will not be an MD5 digest (see `source_hash` instead).
- **force_destroy** (boolean) - Optional - Whether to allow the object to be deleted by removing any legal hold on any object version. Default is `false`. This value should be set to `true` only if the bucket has S3 object lock enabled.
- **kms_key_id** (string) - Optional - ARN of the KMS Key to use for object encryption. If the S3 Bucket has server-side encryption enabled, that value will automatically be used. If referencing the `aws_kms_key` resource, use the `arn` attribute. If referencing the `aws_kms_alias` data source or resource, use the `target_key_arn` attribute. Terraform will only perform drift detection if a configuration value is provided.
- **metadata** (map) - Optional - Map of keys/values to provision metadata (will be automatically prefixed by `x-amz-meta-`, note that only lowercase label are currently supported by the AWS Go API).
- **object_lock_legal_hold_status** (string) - Optional - [Legal hold](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/object-lock-overview.html#object-lock-legal-holds) status that you want to apply to the specified object. Valid values are `ON` and `OFF`.
- **object_lock_mode** (string) - Optional - Object lock [retention mode](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/object-lock-overview.html#object-lock-retention-modes) that you want to apply to this object. Valid values are `GOVERNANCE` and `COMPLIANCE`.
- **object_lock_retain_until_date** (string) - Optional - Date and time, in [RFC3339 format](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3339#section-5.8), when this object's object lock will [expire](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/object-lock-overview.html#object-lock-retention-periods).
- **override_provider** (object) - Optional - Override provider-level configuration options. See [Override Provider](#override-provider) below for more details.

### Request Example
```hcl
resource "aws_s3_object" "example" {
  bucket = "my-example-bucket"
  key    = "my-object-key.txt"
  content = "Hello, S3!"
  acl    = "private"
  tags = {
    Environment = "Dev"
  }
}
```

### Attributes Reference
#### Exported Attributes
- **arn** (string) - The ARN of the object.
- **version_id** (string) - A unique version ID for the object.
- **etag** (string) - The ETag of the object.
- **id** (string) - The `key` of the object.

#### Example Attributes
```json
{
  "arn": "arn:aws:s3:::my-example-bucket/my-object-key.txt",
  "version_id": null,
  "etag": "d41d8cd98f00b204e9800998ecf8427e",
  "id": "my-object-key.txt"
}
```
