### Integrate CloudFront Invalidation into CI/CD Pipeline with Terraform

Source: https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.33.0/website/docs/actions/cloudfront_create_invalidation.html.markdown

Provides an example of integrating CloudFront cache invalidation into a CI/CD pipeline, triggering it after static asset deployment (e.g., S3 sync). It invalidates specific paths relevant to a deployment.

```terraform
# Trigger invalidation after S3 sync
resource "terraform_data" "deploy_complete" {
  input = local.deployment_id

  lifecycle {
    action_trigger {
      events  = [before_create, before_update]
      actions = [action.aws_cloudfront_create_invalidation.post_deploy]
    }
  }

  depends_on = [aws_s3_object.assets]
}

action "aws_cloudfront_create_invalidation" "post_deploy" {
  config {
    distribution_id = aws_cloudfront_distribution.main.id
    paths = [
      "/index.html",
      "/manifest.json",
      "/static/js/*",
      "/static/css/*"
    ]
  }
}
```

### Action: aws_cloudfront_create_invalidation

Source: https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws/blob/v6.33.0/website/docs/cdktf/python/actions/cloudfront_create_invalidation.html.markdown

`aws_cloudfront_create_invalidation` is currently in beta. Its interface and behavior may change as the feature evolves, and breaking changes are possible. It is offered as a technical preview without compatibility guarantees until Terraform 1.14 is generally available. This action invalidates CloudFront distribution cache for specified paths by creating an invalidation request and waiting for it to complete.

